We are redesigning The Flirt Blueprint / F-Formula website from the ground up.

This is an established dating/flirting education brand with years of history. The goal is NOT to make it look like a new SaaS startup, dating app, sex site, or generic modern landing page.

The new experience should feel like:

EDITORIAL LUXURY × MODERN RELATIONSHIP EDUCATION × SENSUAL CONFIDENCE

The design must communicate maturity, authority, intimacy, confidence, and sophistication.

IMPORTANT:

* Do not build the entire website yet.
* For this task, build ONLY the global visual foundation, navigation, and hero section.
* We will build the remaining sections incrementally afterward.
* Do not invent product claims, testimonials, statistics, credentials, or guarantees.
* Preserve the business's established identity while modernizing its digital presentation.
* The existing giant promotional video is an important asset. We control its presentation completely; do not simply embed it in its old layout.

TECHNICAL FOUNDATION

Use the existing project stack where possible.

Create a clean, production-quality frontend that can eventually be deployed on Render.

Use reusable components and design tokens rather than hardcoding styles repeatedly.

Establish CSS variables/design tokens for:

* colors
* typography
* spacing
* border radius
* shadows
* container widths
* transitions

Do not introduce unnecessary dependencies.

VISUAL DIRECTION

The site should NOT look:

* like SaaS
* like a dating app
* like a pornography/adult site
* like an "alpha male" pickup website
* like a cheap coaching funnel
* like a generic Webflow template
* like a startup landing page
* overly feminine
* overly masculine
* excessively red/black
* visually loud

Instead, create a restrained editorial aesthetic.

COLOR SYSTEM

Start with this direction:

Background:

* warm ivory / soft cream

Primary text:

* near-black charcoal

Primary accent:

* deep burgundy / wine

Secondary accent:

* muted rose / dusty mauve

Supporting neutral:

* warm taupe

Do not use bright red.

Do not use purple gradients.

Do not use neon colors.

Do not create gradient backgrounds unless specifically requested later.

The page should feel tactile and warm rather than digital and synthetic.

TYPOGRAPHY

Use a sophisticated editorial serif for major display headlines and a modern neutral sans-serif for body/UI.

Potential direction:

* Display: Instrument Serif, Cormorant Garamond, or DM Serif Display
* UI/body: Inter, Manrope, or Plus Jakarta Sans

Choose the combination that produces the most sophisticated result.

Typography should have:

* strong hierarchy
* generous line-height
* intentional tracking
* large editorial headlines
* restrained body copy

Do not use oversized typography simply for visual spectacle.

GLOBAL LAYOUT

Use a generous max-width container.

Desktop should feel spacious and editorial rather than compressed.

Use asymmetric compositions where appropriate.

Avoid excessive cards.

Avoid putting every piece of content inside a rounded rectangle.

Avoid the modern SaaS pattern of:
icon → rounded card → heading → paragraph → shadow.

The visual system should rely more on:

* typography
* whitespace
* photography/video
* scale
* alignment
* subtle borders
* controlled contrast

NAVIGATION

Create a minimal premium navigation.

Structure:

Left:
FLIRT BLUEPRINT

Center/right:
The F-Formula
About
Results
FAQ

Primary CTA:
GET THE FORMULA

Keep the navigation visually light.

Use a subtle bottom border or extremely restrained separation.

Do not make the navbar huge.

Do not use a giant hamburger menu on desktop.

On mobile:

* brand remains visible
* compact menu trigger
* CTA remains accessible
* navigation should feel intentional, not like a generic mobile template

The navigation may become sticky after scrolling, but keep the sticky state subtle.

HERO

The hero is the most important section.

Do NOT reproduce the current website's old hero structure.

The hero should feel like the opening spread of a premium editorial publication.

Use an asymmetric composition.

Suggested structure:

LEFT / PRIMARY CONTENT:

Small eyebrow:
THE F-FORMULA

Large headline:

"Flirting isn't about having the perfect line.
It's about knowing what happens next."

Supporting copy:

"A practical framework for creating chemistry, reading the moment, and knowing when to move the interaction forward."

Primary CTA:
EXPLORE THE F-FORMULA

Secondary interaction:
WATCH THE INTRO

RIGHT / VISUAL:

Create a large cinematic video composition.

The video should NOT feel like an ordinary YouTube embed.

Treat it as a major visual asset.

The video can be any aspect ratio required by the design.

Use a large editorial video frame with:

* carefully chosen aspect ratio
* subtle border radius around 12–16px
* restrained shadow
* cinematic crop
* custom play button
* custom overlay treatment
* no ugly default player styling visible before interaction

The video should feel closer to a campaign film / editorial image than a standard embedded video.

IMPORTANT VIDEO RULES:

* Do not distort the source video.
* Preserve its natural aspect ratio.
* Use object-fit: cover only where intentional cropping improves composition.
* Never crop important faces/content.
* Do not autoplay with sound.
* If autoplay is used, it must be muted and playsinline.
* Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
* Lazy-load where appropriate.
* Ensure mobile performance remains good.

HERO COMPOSITION

Do not make this a generic 50/50 two-column layout.

Experiment with controlled overlap and asymmetry.

The video can extend beyond the hero grid slightly.

The headline and video should visually interact.

Possible composition:

Headline occupies approximately 45% of the visual field.

Video occupies approximately 55–60%.

Video can overlap the lower boundary of the hero.

The next section should begin visually underneath the video rather than simply appearing after a conventional section boundary.

The result should feel art-directed.

HERO DETAILS

Add a small metadata line beneath the CTA such as:

3 PHASES · PRACTICAL FRAMEWORK · LIFETIME ACCESS

ONLY use metadata that is actually confirmed in the existing product information. If these details are not available in the current code/content, leave the area as a clearly marked placeholder rather than inventing claims.

Do not use fake urgency.

Do not add countdown timers.

Do not add fake notification popups.

Do not add "X people are viewing this."

Do not add fake scarcity.

Do not add floating sales widgets.

Do not add excessive badges.

ANIMATION

Motion should be subtle and premium.

Use:

* gentle fade/slide entrance
* slight stagger between eyebrow, headline, copy, CTA
* subtle video reveal
* understated hover states

Avoid:

* bouncing
* excessive parallax
* spinning elements
* dramatic text animations
* typewriter effects
* scroll-jacking
* excessive blur animations

The page should still feel premium with all animations disabled.

RESPONSIVE DESIGN

Desktop:

* full editorial composition
* large typography
* large cinematic video
* generous whitespace

Tablet:

* reduce typography
* preserve asymmetry where practical
* maintain visual hierarchy

Mobile:

* do NOT simply shrink the desktop layout
* stack the hero intentionally
* headline first
* supporting copy
* CTA
* video
* metadata

The video should become a strong full-width visual element on mobile.

Mobile spacing should feel generous.

Do not allow text to become cramped.

Do not allow horizontal overflow.

ACCESSIBILITY

Use semantic HTML.

Use proper heading hierarchy.

Ensure keyboard navigation.

Ensure visible focus states.

Ensure sufficient text contrast.

Provide accessible video controls.

Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

Use descriptive aria-labels where necessary.

QUALITY BAR

Before considering this complete, inspect the result as if it were being presented to the owner of a successful established brand.

Ask:

"Does this look like a business that has existed for years and is now entering its next chapter?"

NOT:

"Does this look like a cool website?"

It should feel established, intentional, sensual, sophisticated, and expensive without looking pretentious.

IMPORTANT — DO NOT BUILD THE REST OF THE PAGE.

Only implement:

1. Global design tokens
2. Typography foundation
3. Navigation
4. Hero
5. Video presentation
6. Responsive behavior

After implementation, stop and report:

* files changed
* components created
* fonts used
* design tokens created
* video behavior
* any assumptions made

Do not continue into the next sections until instructed.
